Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/keel-linux/keel-pve.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/keel-linux/keel-pve
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: keel-pve
Architecture: all
Depends:
 keel-archive-keyring (>= 0.1.1),
 sqv,
 curl,
 ${misc:Depends},
Enhances: pve-manager
Description: Signed Keel Linux container templates on a Proxmox VE host
 keel-pve fetches the Keel Linux template index, verifies its signature
 with sqv against the Keel archive key from keel-archive-keyring, the way
 pveam verifies its own sources, and downloads a chosen template into the
 vztmpl content of a Proxmox VE storage. A template is kept only when its
 sha512 matches the signed index, and it is written under the file name
 the index gives, so pct create and the Create CT dialog of the web UI
 use it like any other template.
 .
 The Keel templates do not appear in the Templates download dialog of the
 web UI: its sources are fixed in pve-manager, and this package changes
 no pve-manager file.
 .
 It installs an apt pin, /etc/apt/preferences.d/keel-pve, under which the
 Keel archive provides only keel-pve and keel-archive-keyring to the host.
 A daily keel-pve-update.timer is shipped disabled.
